            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "garlic",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "clove",
              "prepNote": "finely grated",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rinse the sliced onion under cold running water in a colander for 30 seconds. This removes some of the sharpness. Drain and set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Place the fish cubes in a non-metallic bowl. Add the lime juice, lemon juice and grated garlic. Toss gently to coat every piece."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the sliced chilli and onion. Stir gently to combine."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cover and refrigerate for exactly 15 minutes. The fish should look opaque on the outside but remain slightly translucent at the centre."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Scatter with coriander leaves and serve immediately in chilled bowls. Include the marinade liquid. Serve alongside sweet potato slices or boiled corn if available."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Fish is rubbery and overcooked-tasting"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The fish sat in the marinade too long. Serve at the 15-minute mark. Acid from citrus denatures the protein the same way heat does, and it continues working the longer the fish sits."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Ceviche tastes too sharp"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Balance the acidity with a small amount of extra-virgin olive oil drizzled over before serving. Remove some of the chilli if the heat is overpowering."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Fish is still raw-tasting after 15 minutes"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Leave for another 5 minutes. Smaller cubes cure faster. If the fish pieces are larger than 2 cm, increase to 20 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Peru considers ceviche a national treasure. Lima has cevichers open from early morning, serving it as a breakfast dish. The Peruvian version is younger, sharper, and more minimalist than Mexican or Ecuadorian ceviche. In 2004 the Peruvian government declared it part of the national cultural heritage. The dish has now spread to every continent."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
